WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.450 --> 00:00:09.910
One evening Monod walked into the lab looking tired and worried, stood silently at a

2
00:00:09.910 --> 00:00:15.470
bench, and told his colleague Agnès Ullmann, "I think I have discovered the second

3
00:00:15.470 --> 00:00:16.490
secret of life."

4
00:00:17.400 --> 00:00:23.260
A biologist who preferred thinking to tinkering, shaping theories with a pipe while

5
00:00:23.260 --> 00:00:29.420
others ran the bench, he had intuited that proteins are not rigid machines but

6
00:00:29.420 --> 00:00:34.940
flexible structures with two kinds of site: one that does the work and one that

7
00:00:34.940 --> 00:00:37.360
controls whether the work can happen at all.

8
00:00:37.360 --> 00:00:42.080
He named the effect allostery but had no mechanism for it.

9
00:00:42.833 --> 00:00:49.573
The picture met its proof when he and the thermodynamicist Jeffries Wyman met over a

10
00:00:49.573 --> 00:00:56.293
blackboard at the Institut Pasteur in 1964: the biologist had the picture and no

11
00:00:56.293 --> 00:01:00.253
proof, the thermodynamicist had the proof and no picture.

12
00:01:01.317 --> 00:01:07.737
Out came the austere two-state MWC model, written with the young Jean-Pierre

13
00:01:07.737 --> 00:01:09.657
Changeux in 1965.

14
00:01:10.750 --> 00:01:16.250
It made sudden sense of the Bohr effect, where acid from working muscle tips

15
00:01:16.250 --> 00:01:21.950
hemoglobin toward the tense state so oxygen falls out exactly where a straining

16
00:01:21.950 --> 00:01:22.950
muscle needs it.
